"Translate",dg_unl:"Upcoming unlocks",dg_unl_of:"{p} of supply",dg_v_bear:"Leaning bearish: {s} of {n} signals",dg_v_bull:"Leaning bullish: {b} of {n} signals",dg_v_mix:"Mixed signals: {b} bullish, {s} bearish",dg_views:"Views: {n}",dg_wallets:"{n} wallets",dg_window:"24 hours to {t}",dm_24h:"24h",dm_30d:"30 days",dm_7d:"7 days",dm_90d:"90 days",dm_all:"Show all {n}",dm_alt_days:"Since {d}: altseason on {a} of {n} days, Bitcoin season on {b}.",dm_alt_peak:"Index peak: {v} ({d}).",dm_alt_title:"Altseason Index",dm_alt_what:"{n} of the 100 largest coins (excluding stablecoins) rose more than Bitcoin over 90 days.",dm_alts:"Altcoins",dm_alts_ex:"Altcoins excl. stablecoins",dm_btc:"Bitcoin",dm_chart:"Bitcoin vs altcoins",dm_chart_hint:"Top: market cap of Bitcoin and of altcoins excluding stablecoins. Bottom: market shares — the top edge of the orange band is the dominance.",dm_dom:"Bitcoin dominance",dm_eb_pos:"Since {d}, ETH/BTC was higher than now on {p} of days.",dm_eb_range:"High {hi} ({hd}), low {lo} ({ld}).",dm_eb_what:"BTC per 1 ETH",dm_err:"Couldn't load the dominance data.",dm_eth:"Ethereum",dm_ex:"Excluding stablecoins:",dm_ex_hint:"Stablecoins are parked dollars, not a bet on altcoins. Without them you see how Bitcoin fares against real altcoins.",dm_flow_alt:"Altcoins did better.",dm_flow_btc:"Bitcoin did better.",dm_flow_eq:"They moved almost in step.",dm_how_1:"Dominance is Bitcoin's share of the whole crypto market cap. It rises when money flows into Bitcoin or altcoins fall harder, and falls in the opposite case.",dm_how_2:"Stablecoins aren't a bet on altcoins. In fear, money moves into dollar tokens and dominance drops with no altseason at all. That's why the share excluding stablecoins is shown alongside.",dm_how_3:"CoinMarketCap's Altseason Index: how many of the 100 largest coins (excluding stablecoins and wrapped tokens) rose more than Bitcoin over 90 days. 75 and above is altseason, 25 and below is Bitcoin season.",dm_how_4:"A wave is a move of Bitcoin's share excluding stablecoins by at least {n} pp without a {n} pp move back. That also gives the level at which the current wave flips.",dm_how_5:"ETH/BTC is how much Bitcoin one ETH costs. Its rise is one of the first signs that money is moving from Bitcoin into altcoins.",dm_less:"Show less",dm_mo:"{n} mo",dm_other:"Other altcoins",dm_p1:"Market cap",dm_p2:"Market shares",dm_pp:"{v} pp",dm_r5y:"5Y",dm_s_alt:"Altseason",dm_s_btc:"Bitcoin season",dm_s_mid:"Neutral",dm_say_alt:"{n} of the top 100 coins beat Bitcoin over 90 days — that's altseason by the CoinMarketCap index.",dm_say_btc:"Only {n} of the top 100 coins beat Bitcoin over 90 days — the market is sticking with Bitcoin.",dm_say_flip_alt:"The wave flips to altcoins if this share drops to {l}.",dm_say_flip_btc:"The wave flips to Bitcoin if this share rises to {l}.",dm_say_flow:"Over 30 days Bitcoin's share excluding stablecoins moved {d}: Bitcoin itself {b}, altcoins excluding stablecoins {a}.",dm_say_mid:"{n} of the top 100 coins beat Bitcoin over 90 days. Altseason starts at 75; Bitcoin season is 25 and below.",dm_say_wave_alt:"The big wave belongs to altcoins: since {d} Bitcoin's share excluding stablecoins fell from {a} to {b}.",dm_say_wave_btc:"The big wave belongs to Bitcoin: since {d} its share excluding stablecoins rose from {a} to {b}.",dm_split:"What the market is made of",dm_src:"Data: CoinMarketCap (market caps, dominance, Altseason Index), DefiLlama and CoinMarketCap (stablecoins), Binance (ETH/BTC). Updated hourly.",dm_st:"Stablecoins",dm_sub:"Whose share of the market is growing — Bitcoin's or the altcoins'. Market caps since 2013, the Altseason Index and the big waves.",dm_title:"Dominance & Altseason",dm_top_n:"Beat it: {n} · lagged: {m}",dm_top_note:"The bar is growth relative to Bitcoin: right of the orange line is better, left is worse. The 100 largest coins from the CoinMarketCap index, stablecoins excluded.",dm_top_title:"Who beat Bitcoin over 90 days",dm_total:"Crypto market cap",dm_w_alt:"Altcoins gained share",dm_w_avg:"Since 2013 there have been {a} altcoin waves (avg. {ad}) and {b} Bitcoin waves (avg. {bd}).",dm_w_btc:"Bitcoin gained share",dm_w_low:"Wave low: {v} ({d}).",dm_w_note:"A wave is a move of Bitcoin's share excluding stablecoins by {n} pp or more. This is history, not a forecast.",dm_w_now:"ongoing",dm_w_peak:"Wave peak: {v} ({d}).",dm_w_title:"Dominance waves",dm_w_today:"now",dm_year:"1 year",dm_yr:"{n} yr",ef_30d_sum:"30 days",ef_7d_sum:"7 days",ef_aum:"assets {v}",ef_by:"Fund flows and assets, daily price:",ef_by_ch:"Coins, totals and holdings are our own calculations.",ef_chart:"Flows and price",ef_chart_d:"Each bar is a day.",ef_chart_keys:"Flow chart: left and right arrows pick a bar",ef_chart_sum:"Bitcoin price and ETF flows for the chosen period, {v} in total. The numbers are in the table below the chart.",ef_chart_w:"Each bar is a week.",ef_cme_am:"Asset managers",ef_cme_basis:"Hedge funds are short and asset managers are long. Usually that's not a bet on a drop: hedge funds hold ETFs or coins and sell the future to earn the price gap — the basis trade.",ef_cme_chart:"Net positions by week",ef_cme_dl:"Dealers and banks",ef_cme_lev:"Hedge funds",ef_cme_ls:"long {l} · short {s}",ef_cme_note:"The CFTC publishes the report on Fridays for the Tuesday. Positions in coins: standard and micro contracts combined. Net = long minus short.",ef_cme_nr:"Small traders",ef_cme_oi:"Open interest",ef_cme_sub:"CME futures per the CFTC report of {d}",ef_cme_title:"Institutions on CME",ef_cme_usd:"≈ {v}",ef_cme_wk:"past week {v}",ef_cum:"Since launch",ef_cum_chart:"Cumulative since launch",ef_cum_hint:"The line is all inflows minus outflows since the funds launched. When it rises, the funds are net buyers.",ef_days_n:"{n} days",ef_err:"Couldn't load ETF data.",ef_f_title:"Who's buying and who's selling",ef_fd_chart:"{t}: daily flows, trading days: {n}, total {v}",ef_fd_days:"Trading days: {n} · total {v}",ef_fd_hold:"Fund holdings",ef_fd_